      <data key="d6">1299</data>
      <data key="d7">243230</data>
      <data key="d8">radA</data>
      <data key="d9">DNA repair protein; DNA-dependent ATPase involved in processing of recombination intermediates, plays a role in repairing DNA breaks. Stimulates the branch migration of RecA-mediated strand transfer reactions, allowing the 3' invading strand to extend heteroduplex DNA faster. Binds ssDNA in the presence of ADP but not other nucleotides, has ATPase activity that is stimulated by ssDNA and various branched DNA structures, but inhibited by SSB. Does not have RecA's homology-searching function. Belongs to the RecA family. RadA subfamily.</data>
      <data key="d10">Q9RVC4</data>
      <data key="d11">Q9RVC4</data>
      <data key="d12">RADA_DEIRA</data>
