      <data key="d8">DR_A0188</data>
      <data key="d9">Excinuclease ABC, subunit A; The UvrABC repair system catalyzes the recognition and processing of DNA lesions. UvrA is an ATPase and a DNA-binding protein. A damage recognition complex composed of 2 UvrA and 2 UvrB subunits scans DNA for abnormalities. When the presence of a lesion has been verified by UvrB, the UvrA molecules dissociate. Belongs to the ABC transporter superfamily. UvrA family.</data>
